{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"turing computable function turing computable function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md","fileName":"Turing-Computable Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Turing-Computable Function","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Turing Machines and Computability]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Turing Machines and Computability","Turing Machine","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"turing computable function turing computable function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Computable Function.md","fileName":"Turing-Computable Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Turing-Computable Function","heading":"Turing-Computable Function","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A function from strings to strings is Turing-computable when a [[Turing Machine]] halts on every input in its domain with the function's value arranged as its output. The machine must therefore both produce the correct string and halt in a defined output configuration.\n\nComputable functions are closed under composition because one machine can compute the first function and then run a machine for the second on that result. This formalizes effective calculation independently of a particular programming language.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Turing Machines and Computability","Turing Machine","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full N